WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.912
"Taurine Supplementation Increases Lifespan
and Healthspan in Animals"

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.880
The level of taurine
in the bodies

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:11.680
of mice, monkeys,
and men, and women,

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:12.960
declines with age,

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:15.680
dropping by nearly 80 percent
over the lifespan.

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.840
This is due, in rats at least,

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:21.200
to a decline
in the synthesis of taurine.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.320
Would there be any benefit
to restoring youthful levels

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.000
through taurine supplementation?

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.840
After all,
lower taurine levels

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:28.720
have been associated

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:30.320
with all sorts
of disease conditions

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:33.520
of the bone, blood,
eyes, heart, cancer.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.360
Of course, just because
there's a correlation

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:37.040
between lower levels and disease

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:39.760
doesn't necessarily mean that
lower levels cause disease.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:41.120
It could be
the other way around,

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:45.760
where, for example, disease
leads to lower taurine levels.

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:47.840
In my last video,
I talked about how taurine

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:50.640
is an antioxidant
in the context of inflammation.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:52.160
So, in the context of disease,

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:54.560
more taurine
may just get used up.

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:56.400
The only way to know
if taurine may help

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.760
is to put it to the test.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:03.600
We know blood concentrations
of taurine declines with age.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.760
So, to investigate
whether this decline

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:08.880
contributes to aging,
researchers fed taurine,

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.720
or not,
to middle-aged mice

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:12.240
until the end of their life.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:16.240
And taurine-fed mice
lived longer,

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:17.360
significantly longer,

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:20.560
like, the human equivalent
of seven to eight years longer.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:22.240
And they had only
started the taurine

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:24.480
later in life,
in middle-age.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:27.200
Now, a meaningful
anti-aging therapy

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:30.400
should not only improve
lifespan but also healthspan,

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.240
the period of healthy living.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:33.920
So, researchers
then investigated

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:36.320
the health of the
taurine-fed middle-aged mice

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.480
and found,
compared to the control group,

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:42.240
improved functioning of bone,
muscle, pancreas, brain, fat,

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:43.520
gut, and immune system,

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:45.120
indicating an overall increase

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:48.080
in healthspan
as well as lifespan.

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:51.280
They also tried it
on other species.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:53.360
Taurine didn't
make yeast live longer,

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:54.800
but it did increase
the lifespan

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.720
of microscopic worms.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:59.440
Ten percent or more
increased average lifespan

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:01.440
in middled-aged worms and mice,

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:03.120
and the mice
didn't just live longer

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:04.560
but also healthier,
with improvements

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:06.640
in strength,
coordination, and memory,

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:09.760
as well as attenuation
of multiple hallmarks of aging

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:11.600
such as cellular senescence,

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:13.280
DNA damage,
and chronic inflammation,

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:15.600
many of the aging pathways
I talked about

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:18.160
in my longevity book,
How Not to Age.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:21.600
And in middle-aged
rhesus macaque monkeys,

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.440
six months
of taurine supplementation

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:26.080
led to positive effects
on bone health, metabolism,

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.520
and apparent immune health.

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:29.280
There were similar
health effects in monkeys

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:31.600
who were the middle-age
equivalent of a human

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:34.240
about 45 to 50 years old,

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:38.160
but that's still
15 years for a monkey,

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:39.040
which is why it's so hard

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:41.360
to do longevity experiments
on monkeys.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.200
If you're a microscopic worm,

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:44.800
"middle-age" is just two weeks,

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:46.400
so, it's a lot easier.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.160
But, researchers did find

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:50.400
that even just six months
of extra taurine

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.280
had beneficial effects
on most tested health parameters

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:55.520
in middle-aged monkeys,

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:57.360
including one or two
fewer pounds (450 or 900 g)

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.360
of weight gain,
better bone mineral density,

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:00.320
better blood sugars,

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:03.440
and lower measures
of inflammation and oxidation.

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:05.840
If you take people,
and have them exercise,

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:07.200
at least in active individuals,

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.040
exercise increases
the concentration

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:10.160
of taurine in the blood.

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:12.160
So, that might even
partially explain

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:14.480
the anti-aging
effects of exercise.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:16.720
The bottom line is that
taurine supplementation

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:18.720
makes animals live longer,

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:22.960
but what that means
for people is unclear.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:24.080
This is not the first time

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:25.600
benefits
of taurine supplementation

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:27.360
have been demonstrated
in lab animals,

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:29.200
reducing blood pressure in rats

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:32.160
or reducing atherosclerosis
in the coronary arteries

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:34.400
of rabbits fed cholesterol.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.080
But the extrapolation
of findings

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:37.920
from animal studies
is difficult,

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:40.240
due to problems
not only with dosing

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:42.560
but the biological
differences between species.

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:44.160
For example, the final step

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:46.080
in taurine synthesis
in rodents

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.160
involves a completely
different enzyme

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:49.760
than in people,
and is actually

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:52.720
much more efficient
in them than in us.

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:55.360
But maybe it needs
to be so much more efficient

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:56.320
because the normal levels

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:58.080
in the blood
and brains of rodents

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:00.400
may be as much
as ten times higher,

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:02.080
potentially making them
more susceptible

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:04.800
to problems with
slipping levels as they age.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:06.560
Unfortunately, little
is known about the effects

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:09.440
of taurine
supplementation in humans.

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:12.880
Here's a graphical
illustration of the study.

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:15.120
Taurine levels
decrease with age,

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:17.840
and taurine supplementation
to reverse this trend

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:19.680
can increase
the lifespan of animals

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:22.560
by countering
the many drivers of aging

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:25.360
and boosting health
in the process.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.360
In people,
lower taurine levels

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:31.200
correlate with worse health,
but the missing piece,

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:34.640
a randomized clinical trial
of taurine in people.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:37.440
What should we do while we wait?

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:40.240
Correction of late-life
taurine decline in humans

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:43.040
could be beneficial
for cognitive performance,

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:45.520
energy metabolism,
sexual function, and vision,

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:49.200
but clinical studies
remain to be performed.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:51.840
There have been some short-term
randomized controlled trials

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:53.680
of taurine supplementation
in people.

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:58.285
And I'll run through
what they found, next.

